  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 208 PM CDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nAn upper level ridge continues to track westward across New Mexico \nand Arizona Friday. Despite the westward shift, the ridge also looks \nto strengthen Friday, pushing highs a few degrees over Thursday's. \nHeat Advisories may be needed for at least the higher terrain Friday \nafternoon. Highs are progged to reach the upper 90s within the \nhigher terrain and Lower Trans Pecos, with triple digits elsewhere. \nThe hottest conditions will be near/along the river valleys, \nespecially the Rio Grande, where highs shall top out at 105-111 \ndegrees. A transient shortwave impulse may trigger isolated shower/ \nstorm development across the northern Permian Basin and SE NM Friday \nevening. \n\nSlightly cooler temperatures and increased rain chances arrive with \na cold front on Saturday. The front sweeps in courtesy of an upper \ntrough expected to dig into the eastern half of the US this weekend. \nRain chances across the area Saturday range from 10-40%, with the \nbest odds over SE NM. Low (10-30%) rain chances shift toward the \nDavis Mountains and Big Bend Sunday afternoon. Meanwhile, highs in \nthe 90s are forecast to be more commonplace Saturday afternoon \nbehind the front. By Sunday, triple digit heat (100-105 degrees) \nbecomes restricted to the Rio Grande Valley. Hot and dry conditions\nreturn Monday and Tuesday, as highs rebound into the upper 90s to\nup to 105F. Highs mainly cool into the 70s each night.",
